==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|knacken}}, probably ultimately related to {{der|de|gmw-pro|*knokōn|t=to knock}}. Related to {{cog|gml|knaken}}, {{m|gml|knakken}}, {{m|gml|knacken}}, {{cog|nds-de|knacken}}. Compare also {{cog|gml|knicken|t=to bend, snap}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|de|De-knacken.ogg}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb}}

# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to make a cracking sound
#: {{syn|de|knacksen}}
#: {{uxi|de|Die Wurst '''knackte''' beim Reinbeissen.|The sausage made a cracking sound when bitten.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[crack]] (open)
#: {{uxi|de|Er '''knackte''' die Nuss.|He '''cracked''' the nut.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|figuratively}} to crack (a mystery, secret, etc.); to [[persuade]] (to reveal something)
#: {{uxi|de|Sie '''knackte''' den Code.|She '''cracked''' the code.}}
#: {{uxi|de|Ich kann ihn '''knacken'''.|I can get him to open up.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[pick]] (a lock)
# {{lb|de|intransitive|chiefly|Germany|regional|informal}} to sleep
#: {{uxi|de|Mach' nicht solchen Lärm, er '''knackt''' gerade.|Don't make such a noise, he's '''sleeping'''.}}

